00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:48.850
and cold calls, well believe it or not

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.480
even though you're working less,

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:53.410
you'll be far more prepared
than using the standard method.

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:54.920
You'll already have a good idea of

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.500
what the professor wants you
to take away from the case.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.750
And you'll remember the facts of the case

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.350
and between the two that's
90% of what the professor

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:03.540
is looking for anyway.

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.860
So use the flipped case method.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:08.000
You'll be able to breeze
through your homework.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.759
You'll be able to write case briefs

00:05:09.759 --> 00:05:11.910
that will go directly into your outline

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.770
and will better prepare you for class.

